/* DISCOVERY / derivation: the CONFOUNDED TURNPIKE GAP -- from Weber, "Optimal Control Theory with
   Applications in Economics" (2011), Sec 3.5 (infinite-horizon control: turnpike, current-value
   Hamiltonian). A long-horizon optimal trajectory spends almost all its time near a static "turnpike"
   (the Hamiltonian equilibrium / optimal steady state). A CONFOUNDED controller, using the biased
   effect b_obs = b + beta (omitted-variable bias), converges to the WRONG turnpike and pays a per-step
   offset FOREVER. This upgrades result #1d (dynamic horizon regret, previously hand-argued) to a proper
   turnpike argument, and yields a NEW discounted-regret certificate via the current-value Hamiltonian.
   Maxima is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

/* setpoint tracking x_{t+1} = b*u_t ; to hold x = xref the control must be u = xref/b. The confounded
   controller believes the effect is b_obs = b + beta and applies u_conf = xref/b_obs, so the state
   SETTLES at the biased turnpike x_conf = b*u_conf. */
bobs : b + beta$
uconf : xref/bobs$
xconf : b*uconf$
print("true turnpike x_true = xref ; confounded turnpike x_conf = b*xref/(b+beta) =", ratsimp(xconf))$

/* TURNPIKE GAP: the offset the confounded controller pays every step. */
offset : ratsimp(xref - xconf)$
print("turnpike gap offset = xref - x_conf =", offset, " = xref*beta/(b+beta) = O(beta)")$
print("check offset - xref*beta/(b+beta) =", ratsimp(offset - xref*beta/(b+beta)), " (0 confirms)")$

/* per-step regret at the biased turnpike (quadratic tracking weight q); the causal controller pays 0. */
c : q*offset^2$
print("per-step regret c = q*offset^2 =", c, " (paid every step; causal controller pays 0)")$

/* (B) UNDISCOUNTED cumulative regret over horizon T = T*c -> infinity (LINEAR, turnpike-grounded).
   This sharpens result #1d: the confounded trajectory is near x_conf for Theta(T) steps (turnpike
   property), each costing c, so cumulative regret grows without bound. */
print("undiscounted cumulative regret R(T) = T*c -> infinity (linear in the horizon)")$

/* (C) DISCOUNTED cumulative regret via the current-value Hamiltonian (discount factor g in (0,1)):
   sum_{t=0}^{T-1} g^t * c = c*(1 - g^T)/(1 - g)  <=  c/(1-g)  < infinity.  So discounting makes the
   confounded regret FINITE even though the undiscounted version is unbounded -- a new certificate. */
Dclosed : c*(1 - g^T)/(1 - g)$
print("discounted R_g(T) = sum g^t c = c*(1-g^T)/(1-g) =", Dclosed, " <= c/(1-g) (finite)")$
/* verify the geometric-sum identity symbolically for a few T */
Dsum(TT) := sum(g^t * c, t, 0, TT-1)$
print("check T=3: sum - closed =", ratsimp(Dsum(3) - subst(T=3, Dclosed)), " (0 confirms geometric sum)")$
print("check T=5: sum - closed =", ratsimp(Dsum(5) - subst(T=5, Dclosed)), " (0 confirms)")$
print("limit T->inf of R_g = c/(1-g) =", ratsimp(limit(Dclosed, T, inf)), " (assuming 0<g<1)")$
